      "writtenOn": "2022-05-11T10:44:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per discussion: if by any chance there is OEM code that is using reflection to access one of the hidden bootclasspath classes defined in this JAR (e.g., android.net.TcpSocketKeepalive), then that code could break.\n\nOEMs should never be doing this, but for safety, we might want to add these classes to the exclude list and ask OEMs to test? We could ensure that the FRC (which is heavily tested by OEMs on T) won\u0027t have the exclude list, by only merging the exclude list into tm-mainline-prod and not tm-dev. This has the following effect:\n- On T devices, the the FRC has the full jarjar rename and the first update after it does not. This is almost certainly safe, because any OEM that has code that refers to the old name would not work.\n- On R and S devices, the classes will not be renamed at all. We can give OEMs a heads up and some time to audit/test (e.g., a couple of months) and then remove the exclude list.\n\nThis is less of a problem for libraries we depend on (e.g., BitUtils) because the OEM will simply be using the framework copy. It\u0027s also less of a problem with the service-connectivity classes because AIUI those are loaded using a different classloader.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 106,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 106,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "d8c0ebac5b511f9098c22b582b4f9e3d4dd96bc7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
